Let me recall the criteria again:                                                                                       
- Diagnostic accuracy studies                                                                                           
- Symptomatic or asymptomatic nonpregnant women and men reproductive age                                                
- Prospective enrollment of participants                                                                                
- No previous diagnostic testing, co-infections or complications                                                        
- Consecutive or random sampling at primary or secondary care facilities                                                
- All participants received index test and reference standard                                                           
- Studies presenting 2x2 data                                                                                           
- Exclude diagnostic case-control studies                                                                               
                                                                                                                        
I'll go study by study:                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                        
